<body>
  <section class="slide"><div class="deck-bg"></div><div class="slide-content">
    <div class="kicker">DeepSeek Technical Briefing</div>
    <h1>DeepSeek-V2: Efficient MoE Language Model with Multi-Head Latent Attention</h1>
    <p style="max-width: 88ch;">A Strong, Economical, and Efficient MoE Language Model</p>
    <div class="metrics">
      <div class="panel metric"><div class="v">236B / 21B</div><div class="l">Total / Activated Parameters</div></div>
      <div class="panel metric"><div class="v">128K</div><div class="l">Context Length</div></div>
      <div class="panel metric"><div class="v">MLA + DeepSeekMoE</div><div class="l">Core Innovations</div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Audience: ML researchers, NLP engineers, graduate students • Based on DeepSeek-V2 paper benchmarks</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="deck-bg"></div><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>The LLM Scaling Dilemma: Performance vs. Cost and Speed</h2>
    <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:clamp(0.6rem,1vh,1rem);">
      <div class="panel">
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Larger dense models improve reasoning and benchmark quality, but training cost scales steeply.</li>
          <li>Autoregressive decoding is bottlenecked by KV cache growth with sequence length.</li>
          <li>Conventional MHA/GQA/MQA trade quality for cache efficiency but still leave large memory pressure.</li>
          <li>Need architecture-level efficiency: sparse activation in FFN + compressed attention state.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <p><strong>DeepSeek-V2 objective</strong>: shift the Pareto frontier by co-designing attention and MoE routing.</p>
        <p class="small">Target outcome: preserve top-tier open-source performance while reducing training and serving costs enough for broad deployment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="deck-bg"></div><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>DeepSeek-V2 Architecture: MLA + DeepSeekMoE in Each Block</h2>
    <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:clamp(0.5rem,1vh,0.8rem);">
      <div class="panel">
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Transformer blocks replace standard attention with <strong>Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA)</strong>.</li>
          <li>Dense FFN is replaced by <strong>DeepSeekMoE</strong> with shared and routed experts.</li>
          <li>Model scale: 236B total parameters with only 21B activated per token.</li>
          <li>Supports 128K context and economical large-scale serving.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <img class="fig" src="/app/benchmark/assets/figure_1.jpg" alt="DeepSeek-V2 architecture diagram" />
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="deck-bg"></div><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Multi-Head Latent Attention Compresses KV Cache by 93.3%</h2>
    <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:clamp(0.5rem,1vh,0.9rem);">
      <div class="panel">
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>MLA performs low-rank joint compression of keys/values into latent states.</li>
          <li>Decoupled RoPE preserves positional modeling while enabling compact cache representation.</li>
          <li>Compared with MHA/GQA/MQA, MLA keeps strong quality while dramatically reducing memory.</li>
          <li>Result: <strong>93.3% KV cache reduction</strong>, enabling longer contexts and higher throughput.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <img class="fig" src="/app/benchmark/assets/figure_2.jpg" alt="Attention comparison across MHA GQA MQA MLA" />
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="deck-bg"></div><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>DeepSeekMoE: Fine-Grained Experts + Shared Expert Isolation</h2>
    <div class="panel" style="margin-top:clamp(0.6rem,1vh,0.9rem);">
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>Each MoE layer combines always-on <strong>shared experts</strong> with selectively activated <strong>routed experts</strong>.</li>
        <li>Top-K gating activates a small subset of experts per token for compute efficiency.</li>
        <li>Device-limited routing constrains expert dispatch to reduce cross-device communication overhead.</li>
        <li>Auxiliary load-balancing losses stabilize expert utilization and prevent collapse.</li>
        <li>Shared experts capture common linguistic patterns; routed experts specialize in harder token regimes.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p class="small">This design improves specialization and efficiency while maintaining stable large-scale training dynamics.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="deck-bg"></div><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>42.5% Training Cost Reduction and 5.76× Throughput vs. DeepSeek 67B</h2>
    <div class="two-col" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; margin-top:clamp(0.6rem,1vh,0.9rem);">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3 style="font-size:clamp(1rem,1.8vw,1.35rem); color:#ffcf87;">DeepSeek 67B (baseline)</h3>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Higher training cost</li>
          <li>Larger KV cache footprint</li>
          <li>Lower max generation throughput</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel" style="border-color:rgba(0,240,200,0.45);">
        <h3 style="font-size:clamp(1rem,1.8vw,1.35rem); color:#66f0d4;">DeepSeek-V2</h3>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li><strong>42.5% lower</strong> training cost</li>
          <li><strong>93.3% lower</strong> KV cache</li>
          <li><strong>5.76× higher</strong> max generation throughput</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Relative efficiency metrics from source brief; absolute FLOPs/cache/throughput values are not assumed.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="deck-bg"></div><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>DeepSeek-V2 Leads MMLU at Only 21B Activated Parameters</h2>
    <div class="two-col" style="grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr; margin-top:clamp(0.45rem,1vh,0.8rem);">
      <div class="scatter-box">
        <div class="scatter-grid"></div>
        <div class="pt ds" style="left: 30%; bottom: 84%;">DeepSeek-V2 (21B, 78.5)</div>
        <div class="pt base" style="left: 86%; bottom: 74%;">LLaMA 3 70B (70B, 77.0)</div>
        <div class="pt base" style="left: 52%; bottom: 77%;">Mixtral 8x22B (39B, 77.6)</div>
        <div class="pt base" style="left: 89%; bottom: 64%;">Qwen1.5 72B (72B, 75.6)</div>
        <div class="pt base" style="left: 83%; bottom: 49%;">DeepSeek 67B (67B, 73.0)</div>
        <div class="pt base" style="left: 86%; bottom: 26%;">LLaMA 2 70B (70B, 69.0)</div>
        <div class="pt base" style="left: 18%; bottom: 34%;">Mixtral 8x7B (13B, 70.6)</div>
        <div class="pt base" style="left: 10%; bottom: 9%;">LLaMA 3 8B (8B, 65.0)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Plot axes: MMLU score vs. activated parameters.</li>
          <li>DeepSeek-V2 is on the Pareto frontier: higher quality at much lower activated compute.</li>
          <li>Outperforms larger 70B-class dense baselines despite 21B activation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small">Reference chart aligns with figure_3 benchmark table.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="deck-bg"></div><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>DeepSeek-V2 Chat (RL) Shows Strong Alignment</h2>
    <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:clamp(0.6rem,1vh,0.9rem);">
      <div class="panel">
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Alignment pipeline: SFT on <strong>1.5M</strong> conversational sessions, then GRPO-based RL.</li>
          <li>Focus: robust open-ended dialog quality in English and Chinese.</li>
          <li>Chinese evaluation: outperforms all open-source and most closed-source systems on AlignBench.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <table class="table">
          <tr><th>Benchmark</th><th>Score</th></tr>
          <tr><td>AlpacaEval 2.0 (length-controlled)</td><td>38.9%</td></tr>
          <tr><td>MT-Bench (overall)</td><td>8.97</td></tr>
          <tr><td>AlignBench (overall, Chinese)</td><td>7.91</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="deck-bg"></div><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Key Takeaways: Architecture Innovation Unlocks Efficient Scaling</h2>
    <div class="panel" style="margin-top:clamp(0.7rem,1vh,1rem);">
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li><strong>MLA</strong> is a high-quality attention alternative with <strong>93.3% KV cache reduction</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>DeepSeekMoE</strong> enables a 236B model trained at <strong>42.5% lower cost</strong> than DeepSeek 67B.</li>
        <li><strong>21B activated parameters</strong> are sufficient for top-tier open-source MMLU performance.</li>
        <li><strong>5.76× generation throughput gain</strong> improves deployment practicality at scale.</li>
        <li>Post-training alignment yields competitive multilingual chat performance and strong Chinese results.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Positioning: DeepSeek-V2 sits on a favorable cost-quality Pareto frontier for open-source LLMs.</p>
  </div></section>
</body>
</html>
